.nh
.TH "glab" "1" "Sep 2026" "Auto generated by spf13/cobra" ""

.SH "نام (NAME)"
glab-mr-note-update \- Update the body of a note on a merge request. (EXPERIMENTAL)


.SH "خلاصه دستور (SYNOPSIS)"
\fBglab mr note update [ | ]  [flags]\fP


.SH "توضیحات (DESCRIPTION)"
Replace the body of an existing note on a merge request.

.PP
\fB<note-id>\fR is a numeric note ID, not a hex discussion ID.
You can find note IDs with:
.IP \(bu 2
\fBglab mr note list -F json\fR (the \fB\&.id\fR field)
.IP \(bu 2
Note URLs: \fB\&.../merge_requests/1#note_12345\fR

.PP
You can change only the note body. You cannot move the position of diff notes.

.PP
This feature is an experiment and is not ready for production use.
It might be unstable or removed at any time.
For more information, see
https://docs.gitlab.com/policy/development_stages_support/.


.SH "گزینه‌ها (OPTIONS)"
\fB-m\fP, \fB--message\fP=""
	New note body. If omitted, opens an editor or reads from stdin.


.SH OPTIONS INHERITED FROM PARENT COMMANDS
\fB-h\fP, \fB--help\fP[=false]
	Show help for this command.

.PP
\fB-R\fP, \fB--repo\fP=""
	Select another repository. You can use either OWNER/REPO or GROUP/NAMESPACE/REPO. The full URL or Git URL is also accepted.


.SH "مثال (EXAMPLE)"
.EX
# Update note 12345 on merge request 1 with a new message
glab mr note update 1 12345 -m "Updated comment"

# Update a note on the current branch's merge request, composing in an editor
glab mr note update 12345

# Pipe the new body from stdin
echo "new body" | glab mr note update 1 12345

.EE


.SH "همچنین ببینید (SEE ALSO)"
\fBglab-mr-note(1)\fP
